The Regulation on admission to higher education issued together with Circular No. 09/2020/TT-BGDDT requires successful candidates to submit valid copies of the following documents:

* Academic transcripts;
* Temporary high school graduation certificates for those who passed the school in the year of graduation or high school diplomas for those that graduated in previous years;
* The birth certificate;
* The evidence for the priority policy prescribed in the guiding documents of the Ministry of Education and Training;
* Other requirements as prescribed by the schools.

There is no mention of a duplicate ID in the list of required documents. Therefore, it can be concluded that it is not mandatory to have a duplicate ID in a college application.
